it coming out within the year. It might, but don't count on it. Once it's &amp;quot;In Layout&amp;quot;, it's probably a safe bet that it'll be done in a few months, but you never know, sometimes it's several. Once it hits &amp;quot;Proofing&amp;quot;, then you can start getting hyped about an impending release. You won't get a release date until the Monday before the advance PDF comes out (at which point they'll say &amp;quot;It'll be out on Wednesday&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but that's the point where I let myself get more excited with each passing week. Sometimes that hype train keeps going for a couple months, but I know I've got enough steam for that, and your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> As for Lost 2e specifically? With it still in the &amp;quot;Development&amp;quot; stage (not even post-editing development!) I think Fumus' &amp;quot;early 2017 estimate is very optimistic. If I were to take a shot in the dark, I'd say summer 2017, and I wouldn't even be confident in that estimate. In the mean time, there's been more than enough material previewed to playtest it, or to cobble together a 1.5e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the estimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:51:16-07:00","id":962409,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the guess. Guess I'll have to keep my patience. It's hard because I'm one of the people going 'squee' over a number of changes you're making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:55:17-07:00","id":962411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962409#post962409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the guess. Guess I'll have to keep my patience. It's hard because I'm one of the people going 'squee' over a number of changes you're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know much about it, I decided not to bother buying 1st edition because I love the 2e rules. What are the changes your speaking of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:57:20-07:00","id":962415,"title":"","content":"For the record, I don't work for Onyx Path and my guess is as good as any of yours. Don't start telling your group to brainstorm characters for your summer game or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:46:40-07:00","id":962449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962411#post962411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know much about it, I decided not to bother buying 1st edition because I love the 2e rules. What are the changes your speaking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been a lot of changes made that we've seen. One of the biggest is the interaction between Seeming and Kith. Changeling's C-Splats, Seemings, were further divided into sort of sub-splats called Kiths in 1e. So where in Vampire a Daeva is always a Daeva and a Gangrel is always a Gangrel, in Changeling a Fairest could be a Dancer, or a Draconic, or a Truefriend, or a Muse... There were about a dozen or so Kiths per Seeming in the core book and more were added in later books. Well, in 2e, Kiths are completely independent of Seemings. So, in 1e a Muse was always a Fairest and a Tunnelgrub was always a Darkling, short of Dual Kith shenanigans. Dual Kith was a Merit that (surprise) let you take a second Kith, and pretty much everyone took it, often as a way to get the Kith they wanted that was normally associated with a different Seeming. So, 2e cuts out the middle man and just lets you pair any Kith with any Seeming.<br /> <br /> There's also the standard 1e to 2e updates, like the Integrity stat (Clarity) being reworked, and the powers being re-structured. Another big one is that the Y-splat, Courts, is being made customizable. Where 1e had the 4 seasonal courts in the core book and some additional courts in later books, 2e is getting rules for designing your own courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T15:28:43-07:00","id":962531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962449#post962449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been a lot of changes made that we've seen. One of the biggest is the interaction between Seeming and Kith. Changeling's C-Splats, Seemings, were further divided into sort of sub-splats called Kiths in 1e. So where in Vampire a Daeva is always a Daeva and a Gangrel is always a Gangrel, in Changeling a Fairest could be a Dancer, or a Draconic, or a Truefriend, or a Muse... There were about a dozen or so Kiths per Seeming in the core book and more were added in later books. Well, in 2e, Kiths are completely independent of Seemings. So, in 1e a Muse was always a Fairest and a Tunnelgrub was always a Darkling, short of Dual Kith shenanigans. Dual Kith was a Merit that (surprise) let you take a second Kith, and pretty much everyone took it, often as a way to get the Kith they wanted that was normally associated with a different Seeming. So, 2e cuts out the middle man and just lets you pair any Kith with any Seeming.<br /> <br /> There's also the standard 1e to 2e updates, like the Integrity stat (Clarity) being reworked, and the powers being re-structured. Another big one is that the Y-splat, Courts, is being made customizable. Where 1e had the 4 seasonal courts in the core book and some additional courts in later books, 2e is getting rules for designing your own courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there seems to be a lot more character customization than in vampire. Do your Kiths decide your discipline equiviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:28:24-07:00","id":962554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962531#post962531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So there seems to be a lot more character customization than in vampire. Do your Kiths decide your discipline equiviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your kith doesn't impact on your Contracts (the discipline equivalent), but your Seeming and which Court you're in do. All of the general Contracts have a default effect and a small number of additional little benefits that you can use if your a certain Seeming, and at character creation you have to take at least one Contract that would give you one of those benefits, though you can spend xp to get benefits of a contract associated another seeming. Courts have a small number of associated Contracts, these contracts are cheaper to buy for members of their court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:11:26-07:00","id":962578,"title":"","content":"I know this is getting further off topic, but while we're on the subject, what are x splats, and y splats? Regular splats are just vampires, or changelings right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:53:20-07:00","id":962599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962531#post962531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there seems to be a lot more character customization than in vampire. Do your Kiths decide your discipline equiviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, Contracts (the Discipline equivalent) were pretty much Disciplines by any other name. They were rated from 1-5 dots, each dot was an individual ability, you got a list of Affinity Contracts based on your Seeming that you could buy at a discounted experience cost (Kith didn't normally come into it, but there were some Kiths that gave a small discount on a specific Contract that wasn't Affinity for its Seeming). Then there were Court-specific Contracts that required you to be a member of the appropriate Court or have at least one dot of the Court Good Will Merit in the appropriate Court to learn. Considered Affinity if you were a full member of the Court, non-Affinity if you learned it through Good Will.<br /> <br /> In 2e, Contracts are being totally restructured to differentiate them from Disciplines. Now they work much more like Merits, with each power being an individual Contract instead of lumping them into groups of five escalating powers, and each Contract has a dot rating, with splashier effects costing more dots, and Contracts cost 1 experience per dot. Any character can learn any Contract, but some Contracts have bonus effects tied to certain Seemings. If you have the right Seeming you get the bonus effect for free, and if you're a different Seeming you can learn the bonus effect for one experience if you have a teacher of the right Seeming. Court Contracts are a little different, basically they work like normal Contracts, but some of their effects are variable and depend on your Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-02-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:02:32-07:00","id":962606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962578#post962578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is getting further off topic, but while we're on the subject, what are x splats, and y splats? Regular splats are just vampires, or changelings right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I usually say &quot;templates&quot; instead of &quot;splats&quot; for the type of monster (vampire, werewolf, mage, etc.) to avoid getting the terminology up with what I call X-, Y-, and Z-splats. But, what I refer to as an X-splat is the inborn subsplat for a Template (Clan, Auspice, Path, etc.) What I refer to as a Y-splat is the chosen subsplat for a Template (Covenant, Tribe, Order, etc.) What I refer to as a Z-splat is a further refinement of an X- or Y-splat (Bloodline, Lodge, Legacy, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T05:20:36-07:00","id":962777,"title":"","content":"It's still a little bit away. I've got to do some fixing. There were some things I had to change before it goes over to White Wolf for approval. And while those things seemed like relatively small things, they actually snowballed out and I had to do a lot of minor fusses and tweaks, and test this, that, and the other thing. <br /> <br /> I'll be handing over final text soon. Then, it depends on how long it takes with the editor they hire, and art direction. Some books blow through art direction and layout quickly. Some take a lot of time. It's hard to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T05:42:03-07:00","id":962784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962777#post962777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a little bit away. I've got to do some fixing. There were some things I had to change before it goes over to White Wolf for approval. And while those things seemed like relatively small things, they actually snowballed out and I had to do a lot of minor fusses and tweaks, and test this, that, and the other thing.<br /> <br /> I'll be handing over final text soon. Then, it depends on how long it takes with the editor they hire, and art direction. Some books blow through art direction and layout quickly. Some take a lot of time. It's hard to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're all rooting for you! the open development docs you shared really whet the appetite for Changeling the Lost 2E. Not doubts here that this will be a most excellent book and game. have artists been approached yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":".  PS: and is there any of the minor tweeks you're free to share? 09-03-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:41:34-07:00","id":962853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962777#post962777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a little bit away. I've got to do some fixing. There were some things I had to change before it goes over to White Wolf for approval. And while those things seemed like relatively small things, they actually snowballed out and I had to do a lot of minor fusses and tweaks, and test this, that, and the other thing. <br /> <br /> I'll be handing over final text soon. Then, it depends on how long it takes with the editor they hire, and art direction. Some books blow through art direction and layout quickly. Some take a lot of time. It's hard to say.</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember you saying something about making Changeling's Dreamwalking rules more compatible with Mage/Beasts Dream Form rules, so I can see that being challenging tweaking that for example.<br /> <br /> I'm really curious what other tweaks you've done, and how different the final verison of Changeling: The Lost 2e will be from the playtest documents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:00:32-07:00","id":962864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962606#post962606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I usually say &amp;quot;templates&amp;quot; instead of &amp;quot;splats&amp;quot; for the type of monster (vampire, werewolf, mage, etc.) to avoid getting the terminology up with what I call X-, Y-, and Z-splats. But, what I refer to as an X-splat is the inborn subsplat for a Template (Clan, Auspice, Path, etc.) What I refer to as a Y-splat is the chosen subsplat for a Template (Covenant, Tribe, Order, etc.) What I refer to as a Z-splat is a further refinement of an X- or Y-splat (Bloodline, Lodge, Legacy, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Its alittle more complicated in Changeling, including Changeling 2e.<br /> <br /> In Changeling 2e the X splat is split in 2. You have your Kith which is what your keeper turned you into. And your Seeming, which is how your escape transformed you. Both are innate.<br /> <br /> There are over 100 Kiths and 7 Seemings (Beasts, Darklings, Elementals, Fairest, Orgers, Loyalists, and Wizened, although Loyalist tend to be anatogonists). That's over 700 possible combinations for an X splat right from core.<br /> <br /> The Y splat are Courts when vary depending on Freehold. Miami's Freehold uses a traditional Seasonal Court system, with Autumn, Spring, Winter, and Summer courts. The Toronto Freehold uses a very multicultural verison of the 1001 nights system, with the Brass, Jade, Ivory, and Silver Courts (and possibly Ruby Court). A freehold usually can have 2 to six courts with 2 being the minium). They're will be a variety of example freeholds with different court systems including Toronto, Miami, Budapest, Cape something (Africa), Tokyo, Paris, possibly some others.<br /> <br /> The Z splat (Zed splat I'm Canadian), is Noble/Eldrich Entitlements, which think has been mentioned somewhere as being in the core.<br /> <br /> There is some Changeling 2e material in Dark Eras, but the machanics are mostly in iffy condition, but I'm hoping when Changeling 2e is published they post errata fixing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:17:43-07:00","id":962875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962864#post962864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its alittle more complicated in Changeling, including Changeling 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a little more complicated in every gameline outside Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, but K9ine asked what I meant by X-splat and Y-splat, so I was explaining what the basic terms mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:47:32-07:00","id":963052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=962853#post962853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember you saying something about making Changeling's Dreamwalking rules more compatible with Mage/Beasts Dream Form rules, so I can see that being challenging tweaking that for example.<br /> <br /> I'm really curious what other tweaks you've done, and how different the final verison of Changeling: The Lost 2e will be from the playtest documents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually going to make it as close as possible to those, but of course with some fan notes taken into account and things. <br /> <br /> Largely, the changes were to the dreamwalking rules. There are some implications that I feel really impacted other content. For example, what happens when you die in a dream. <br /> <br /> But I think we've got a phenomenal game, and I hope you all love what we did with it. <br /> <br /> And re: Art - I don't know. I'm not involved in that process. USUALLY artists aren't approached until the words go over to editing. But I think sometimes for core books, they approach past core book artists or whatever. So who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:07:45-07:00","id":963282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=963052#post963052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually going to make it as close as possible to those, but of course with some fan notes taken into account and things. <br /> <br /> Largely, the changes were to the dreamwalking rules. There are some implications that I feel really impacted other content. For example, what happens when you die in a dream. <br /> <br /> But I think we've got a phenomenal game, and I hope you all love what we did with it. <br /> <br /> And re: Art - I don't know. I'm not involved in that process. USUALLY artists aren't approached until the words go over to editing. But I think sometimes for core books, they approach past core book artists or whatever. So who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool. I do hope dream crafting, Incubi/succubi/cambions/Oiernos are still in, and the Too Solid Flesh Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:10:07-07:00","id":963283,"title":"","content":"Actually just a guess, but maybe now the only way to really die in a dream is if a Fae has caused the Too Solid Flesh Tilt, otherwise dying in a dream just causes the soul shocked condition. Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:52:10-07:00","id":963341,"title":"","content":"Since others have covered the general changes, I thought I'd mention why I'm going squee over some of them:<br /> <br /> 1) Seeming being about how you escaped: Having it affect your Clarity really ties it in with your character's method of coping with their trauma. It also gives a feeling that you got something out of Arcadia because of your choices, instead of your Keeper's. I can imagine Changelings taking pride in having a Seeming that runs counter to their Keeper's favorite themes.<br /> <br /> 2) We now have a clear explanation for how the Courts prevent the Fae from just running up and grabbing Changelings, and it seems very appropriate. I think it also illustrates the mindset of the Fae and the Wyrd: Fae are the incarnation of story logic, and are instinctively obligated to keep things interesting. They have to use certain Approaches and beat you at what your Court is good at. Before, the Court system seemed to boil down to confusing the Fae with the process of passing power between Courts, something the Gentry find illogical. That's still an aspect of the Court system, but now we know how the system also protects individual Changelings, rather than just the freehold as a whole.<br /> <br /> 3) The new Clarity system: It reinforces the theme of coping with trauma, now with personalized triggers. Aside from your Seeming's free Clarity, you regain Clarity by facing your triggers and keeping your self-control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T13:47:58-07:00","id":963365,"title":"","content":"&quot;Court Contracts are a little different, basically they work like normal Contracts, but some of their effects are variable and depend on your Court.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't know that (except for emotional contract being tied to the emotion of the court, although I think of those as seperate,but related contracts.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:04:31-07:00","id":963405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=963365#post963365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Court Contracts are a little different, basically they work like normal Contracts, but some of their effects are variable and depend on your Court.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't know that (except for emotional contract being tied to the emotion of the court, although I think of those as seperate,but related contracts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The various emotion Contracts are what I was referring to. I don't think we've seen any other Court Contracts yet, and I merely assumed that they work similarly to the emotion ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:13:31-07:00","id":963410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=963052#post963052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Largely, the changes were to the dreamwalking rules. There are some implications that I feel really impacted other content. For example, what happens when you die in a dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could keep it simple and mostly follow the Mage rules for dying in the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:12:58-07:00","id":963430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=963405#post963405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The various emotion Contracts are what I was referring to. I don't think we've seen any other Court Contracts yet, and I merely assumed that they work similarly to the emotion ones.</div> </div> </div> </div> That does make sense. Dark Eras really didn't explain this, even though we got 2e contracts which is why it will likely need some errata to be compatible with the 2e Changeling Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:19:56-07:00","id":963431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/962279-how-soon-could-we-see-ctl-2e?p=963410#post963410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could keep it simple and mostly follow the Mage rules for dying in the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div> My speculation is that David will use the Mage/Beast rules for dying in a dream, except when the Too Solid Flesh Tilt is up, which changes the nature of the dream to make it more powerful, making real death a possiblity, and turning some objects and creatures (Goetics?) into Fae (Incubi).<br /> <br /> But that is just my GUESS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":